BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Ripeline) Tj T* () Tj T* (Executive Summary: Ripeline) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Fresh produce is the most perishable and one of the most profitable departments in a grocery) Tj T* (store, and independent grocers manage it with far fewer tools than the chains. In conversations) Tj T* (with 14 independent store owners and produce managers in our region, 11 said they order from) Tj T* (memory, handwritten notes, or last week's invoice. Spoilage estimates in the stores we) Tj T* (interviewed ranged from 8 to 14 percent of produce purchases. For a store with $400,000 in) Tj T* (annual produce purchases, a 10 percent loss is roughly $40,000, which can exceed a store's) Tj T* (annual net profit in a tight year.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Two causes recur. First, ordering is imprecise: managers over-order to avoid empty shelves and) Tj T* (rarely know how much sellable life a delivery has left. Second, storage and rotation practices) Tj T* (vary by employee. Staff turnover is high, and most stores have no formal training on) Tj T* (temperature zones, ethylene-sensitive items, or first-in-first-out rotation.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Ripeline combines three components sold as one service.) Tj T* () Tj T* (1. Shelf-life predictor. A model estimates remaining sellable days for each produce item from) Tj T* (its type, delivery date, supplier lead time, and storage conditions \(cooler, backroom, or) Tj T* (display\). It is built on published post-harvest research and refined with data from our pilot) Tj T* (stores.) Tj T* () Tj T* (2. Ordering app. The app takes the predictor's output and recent sales data and suggests order) Tj T* (quantities per item and per delivery day. Managers can accept, adjust, or ignore each) Tj T* (suggestion. The app also flags items nearing end of life so staff can mark them down before) Tj T* (they are lost.) Tj T* () Tj T* (3. Staff training modules. Ten short modules, each about 10 minutes, cover storage conditions,) Tj T* (rotation, markdown timing, and handling of ethylene-producing items. Each ends with a brief) Tj T* (quiz so managers can confirm completion.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The goal is a measurable reduction in spoilage with little added work for managers.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (The United States has roughly 21,000 independent supermarkets and grocery stores according to) Tj T* (industry association figures we have reviewed. We focus on stores with annual sales between $2) Tj T* (million and $15 million, which we estimate at about 8,000 locations, large enough to have) Tj T* (meaningful produce volume but too small for enterprise inventory systems. If 8,000 stores paid) Tj T* ($250 per month, the serviceable market would be about $24 million per year. Our initial target) Tj T* (is the 300 or so qualifying stores within a three-hour drive of our university, where we can) Tj T* (provide in-person onboarding. We have not yet validated these market-size figures independently) Tj T* (and treat them as working estimates.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (Ripeline will charge a monthly subscription tiered by store size: $150 for stores under $3) Tj T* (million in annual sales, $250 for mid-size stores, and $400 for larger stores. Onboarding and) Tj T* (training access are included. We assume a three-month onboarding period during which we offer a) Tj T* (discounted rate. At an average of $250 per month and a hoped-for customer life of three years,) Tj T* (lifetime revenue per store would be about $9,000. Estimated acquisition cost is $1,500 per) Tj T* (store, driven by in-person visits and a part-time field representative. Our gross margin) Tj T* (assumption is 70 percent, mostly cloud hosting and support. These figures are projections; we) Tj T* (have no paying customers yet.) Tj ET
endstream
