BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (The space is crowded. Large retailers use enterprise demand-forecasting platforms that are too) Tj T* (costly and complex for independent stores. Several startups offer food-waste analytics or) Tj T* (markdown software, mostly targeting regional chains. Distributors provide basic online ordering) Tj T* (but no spoilage prediction. Most independents today use spreadsheets or nothing. Our) Tj T* (differentiation is the combination of prediction, ordering, and training at a price an) Tj T* (independent can afford. We recognize that a distributor or an existing analytics vendor could) Tj T* (add similar features, and that our prediction accuracy has not been tested at scale. Our) Tj T* (defensibility today rests on speed, service quality, and the store-level data we accumulate.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Maya Okonkwo-Reyes \(CEO\) is a senior in business administration who worked two summers in her) Tj T* (family's grocery in a mid-size city, where she handled ordering and saw spoilage firsthand. She) Tj T* (leads customer discovery and operations.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Daniel Hartwell \(CTO\) is a senior in computer science with experience building mobile) Tj T* (applications. He built the ordering app and the integration of the prediction model.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Priya Venkataraman \(Head of Data and Training\) is a graduate student in food science and data) Tj T* (analytics. She developed the shelf-life model and wrote the training modules.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have not yet recruited an advisor with grocery industry experience, which we regard as a) Tj T* (gap.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have completed the following: interviews with 14 grocers; a working prototype covering 24) Tj T* (produce items; a pilot in two stores near our university over six weeks; incorporation of) Tj T* (Ripeline Inc. as a Delaware C Corp; and a company website. In the pilot, one store reported) Tj T* (roughly 11 percent less produce discarded relative to its prior six-week average; the other did) Tj T* (not track discards carefully enough to compare. The sample is small, there was no control) Tj T* (group, and results may reflect other factors, so we regard this as encouraging but not proof.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our 12-month plan targets 15 paying stores by month twelve, expanding the model to 60 produce) Tj T* (items, and adding integration with at least one major distributor's ordering portal. Projected) Tj T* (first-year revenue is about $30,000 against expenses of about $85,000 \(stipend for a part-time) Tj T* (field representative, cloud and software costs, travel, and legal and accounting\). We expect to) Tj T* (be pre-profit for at least the first two years. To date the team has funded the venture with) Tj T* (about $4,000 of personal savings.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are seeking a prize or seed award of $25,000 to $40,000 to cover the first nine months: a) Tj T* (part-time field representative, pilot expansion to 10 stores with careful discard tracking, and) Tj T* (independent validation of prediction accuracy. Beyond funding, we would value introductions to) Tj T* (independent grocers' associations, mentors with grocery or distribution experience, and) Tj T* (feedback on our pricing and customer acquisition plan. We believe a modest, disciplined pilot) Tj T* (expansion will tell us whether Ripeline's results hold across more stores and whether grocers) Tj T* (will pay for them.) Tj ET
endstream
